# ─── Media storage ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Plain HTTPS base URLs. Any S3-compatible provider works, so moving from
# Backblaze B2 to Cloudflare R2 later is a change to these two lines only.
# Key layout is identical either way — see src/lib/storage.ts.
#
# Setup walkthrough: docs/setup/07-b2-cloudflare-cdn.md

# Images: thumbnails, storyboard frames, avatars.
#   with CDN:   https://cdn.vidubuzz.com
#   B2 direct:  https://f003.backblazeb2.com/file/vidubuzz-media
NEXT_PUBLIC_IMAGE_BASE=

# Video: the MP4 renditions.
#   with CDN:   https://video.vidubuzz.com
#   B2 direct:  https://f003.backblazeb2.com/file/vidubuzz-video
#
# Kept separate from the image base on purpose. Cloudflare's self-serve terms
# require a paid service to serve video through the CDN, so if they ever flag
# the account you can grey-cloud the video hostname and point this at B2
# directly — images keep their CDN, the site keeps working, no code changes.
NEXT_PUBLIC_VIDEO_BASE=

# Both empty => imageUrl()/videoUrl() return null and the UI falls back to
# generated gradient placeholders. The site builds and runs with no storage.
